# Valgrind suppressions for the duckdb PHP extension test suite.
#
# These cover allocations owned by glibc and libduckdb's thread lifecycle,
# not by extension code: every std::thread pays a one-time TLS slot that the
# dynamic loader keeps until process exit (threads are pooled and reused),
# which Memcheck reports as "possibly lost". Suppressing them keeps the
# valgrind harness stage signal-only — any entry here must name a stack we
# do not own. Extension-owned allocations must never be added.

{
   glibc-thread-tls-dtv
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:calloc
   fun:calloc
   fun:allocate_dtv
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   fun:allocate_stack
   fun:pthread_create*
   ...
}
